    "Condition : 1 - London Borough of Hounslow objects to the planning application on the grounds that the development has the potential to adversely affect the amenity of the adjoining dwelling due to the size and bulk of the proposed development. In particular it is considered that the depth of the extension is excessive and that a staggered extension rather than a 'wrap around' design would be more appropriate. If, notwithstanding this objection, the development is permitted, it is requested that obscured glazing is installed in the proposed utility room window."
